oil|olive oil]]\n*2 cloves [[Cookbook:Garlic|garlic]], [[Cookbook:Chop|chopped]]\n*1 medium [[Cookbook:Onion|onion]], chopped\n*1 can (15 [[Cookbook:Ounce|oz]]) diced [[Cookbook:Tomato|tomatoes]], undrained\n*1 can (15 oz) black-eyed peas, drained\n*¼–½ [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] [[Cookbook:Cayenne Pepper|cayenne pepper]]\n*1 [[Cookbook:Bay Leaf|bay leaf]]\n*1 package (10 oz) frozen [[Cookbook:Kale|kale]], thawed\n*[[Cookbook:Salt|Salt]] to taste\n*[[Cookbook:Pepper|Pepper]] to taste\n\n==Procedure==\n#[[Cookbook:Sautéing|Sauté]] the onion and garlic in the oil over medium heat for several minutes.\n#Add tomatoes and their juice, peas, cayenne and bay leaf. [[Cookbook:Simmering|Simmer]], covered, for 15 minutes.\n#Add kale and simmer uncovered until kale is tender but still green (5–10 minutes). Season to taste with salt and freshly-ground black pepper.\n\n==Nutritional information==\n''Per serving: 210 calories; 10 g protein; 4 g fat; 34 g carbohydrate; 0 mg cholesterol''\n\n[[Category:Recipes using tomato]]\n[[Category:Boiled recipes]]\n[[Category:Vegan recipes]]\n[[Category:Side dish recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using kale]]\n[[Category:Recipes using onion]]\n[[Category:Recipes using garlic]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cowpea]]\n[[Category:Recipes using olive oil]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cayenne]]\n[[Category:Recipes using bay leaf]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Black-Eyed Peas and Kale","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"1 tbsp olive oil","sourceText":"1 tbsp olive oil","amountText":"1 tbsp olive oil","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"2 cloves garlic, chopped","sourceText":"2 cloves garlic, chopped","amountText":"2 cloves garlic, chopped","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"1 medium onion, chopped","sourceText":"1 medium onion, chopped","amountText":"1 medium onion, chopped","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBin